# FinEzy AI Coding Standards (.windsurfrules / .clinerules)

You are an AI assistant working on the FinEzy codebase. Adhere strictly to these rules:

## Technology Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- Vanilla CSS styling (No Tailwind, No Bootstrap)
- Supabase Client SDK (`@supabase/supabase-js`)
- Lucide React for Icons

## Styling & Design Guidelines
- Never hardcode HEX or RGB values. Always use HSL variables from globals.css (e.g., `var(--primary)`, `var(--bg-surface)`).
- Fonts: Apply `--font-heading` (Outfit) for headings, `--font-body` (Inter) for standard elements.
- Corners: Use `--radius-sm` (6px), `--radius-md` (10px), `--radius-lg` (16px), `--radius-xl` (24px).
- Transitions: Apply `--transition-fast` (0.15s), `--transition-normal` (0.25s), or `--transition-slow` (0.4s) on interactive hover/focus states.
- Glassmorphism: Use `var(--glass-bg)`, `var(--glass-border)`, and `backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur))`.

## Coding Best Practices
- Place `"use client"` at the top of client-side interactive component files.
- Handle database transactions securely using client-side environment configs (`process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`).
- Maintain a proper heading structure (single `<h1>` per view, cascading semantic headings).
- Use semantic HTML tags (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<header>`) and unique testable IDs for forms.
</file>

